  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123102,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary\nColonial Pipeline Company\nCollins Butane Blending\n1000 0025 8222\n\nThe Colonial Pipeline Company's, Collins Terminal is refined products storage and distribution facility located in Covington County at 31 Pump Station Road, Collins, MS 39428.\n\nThe facility includes aboveground storage tanks containing various grades of gasoline and other petroleum products. Petroleum products are received and distributed by pipeline these operations are PHMSA jurisdictional. In addition to the petroleum operations, the Collins Terminal also includes a butane blending operation in which butane is received via trucks and blended into gasoline. This document pertains specifically to the butane operations conducted at the Collins Terminal, herein identified as the Butane Blending Process.\n\nThis document has been prepared to meet the regulatory requirements for the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) identified in 29 CFR Part 1910.119 (Process Safety Management of Highly Hazardous Chemicals [PSM]) and the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) identified in 40 CFR Part 68 (Risk Management Plan [RMP]). Those rules have been determined to be applicable to the facility because the Butane Blending Process involves the storage of butane in excess of the identified threshold quantity, 10,000 pounds.\n\nIn addition, the Butane Blending Process has been identified as a Program Level 3 process under the RMP rule. The facility infrastructure and operations beyond the defined butane blending process are related to the storage and transfer of petroleum products and pipeline operations. This equipment and those operations are not included in the PSM/RMP program per Rule and legal interpretation.  \n\nThe butane trucks themselves, the gasoline sampling system, and the nitrogen system that supplies the emergency shutoff valves are not considered part of the PSM/RMP applicable process. Refer to the section below titled Boundaries of the Facility PSM/RMP Applica"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123102,
      "SummaryText": "ble Process for further information.\n\nThe Butane Blending Process consists of a truck offloading skid that can support the simultaneous offloading of two (2) butane transports.  Liquefied butane is offloaded from trucks and pumped/injected directly into inbound lines during pipeline receipt events. The butane injection rate is determined automatically by an in-line gasoline sampling system that periodically measures the vapor pressure of the incoming gas. The PLC uses this information to control the butane injection rate by adjusting the number and speed of the operating pump(s) as well as throttling control valves.\n\nThe Butane Blending Process was designed to meet the requirements of National Fire Protection Association Code No. 58 (NFPA 58) for siting and safety/control functions (2024 edition at the time of installation).  NFPA 58 is identified as the primary \u0093Recognized and Generally Accepted Good Engineering Practice\u0094 (RAGAGEP) for this process. Refer to the section below titled Design Codes and Standards Employed for further information.\n\nEmergency services include on-site incipient stage fire protection (portable fire extinguishers) and coordination with outside agencies including the Collins Fire Department and Covington County Local Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC)."
    }
  ]
